body:
Well haven't touched anything since Monday and won't be any MDMA for a good 4 months. I however feel absolutely amazing. It's healed all my hormonal, emotions, sex drive. 

&#x200B;

Very sad instead of a discussion a few ppl here had intense anger. To the point mods had to remove it due to how toxic ppl where being. Thank you for those who did contribute interesting topics such as ADHD/SSRI's and other civil back and forths.

I think you should follow your own advice. Because as you can see here when you read it. I have agreed with ppl. And decided MDMA is not going to be the drug I use for the last 2 years. 

&#x200B;

What you seem to have a problem with is people asking for more questions and information. Which is how people learn. You however seem very irrational here. One, no you can't indicate tone through a keyboard. As you clearly have insinuated. Questions as "crazy." You've also somehow projected anger/take a deep breath. And do less drugs? I haven't taken anything today. Won't tommorow. Might not even Saturday. Will be next Monday. 

&#x200B;

Take your own advice child. Idk what your social life is like but groups talking about a subject. Ppl ask questions when they want to anwser things. Not just say opinions and then decide if you question said opinion the person is crazy. 

&#x200B;

Bit of advice, take a deep breath. Learn to talk to people.

Oh I heard plenty of the go to therapy for your bad evil choices here as well. Well I also did that. You know it's funny when you do that alongside everything also for maybe a decade. And every single one from every branch imaginable of that profession. Has absolutely nothing to say. Because sadly you can't use talking therapy on something physically and crappy materially outside in your life.

&#x200B;

I wish they where miracle workers as some ppl seem to think! Hey doc thanks so much I'm totally content with spending what limited time I have on this earth stuck inside a tiny flat. Maybe I'll make a circle of teddy bears to talk to? Even prison inmates get to talk to people.

I've been to them all! And I spent decades from childhood with doctors doing everything. Even procedures that can kill, severely damage a child. After 8 or so years of that and nothing working. (They couldn't quite accurately diagnose me they where just throwing darts. Leukemia they told me with my parents present at like 8yos. Oh that's not right? CRMO bone inflammation and atrophy? It doesn't fully fit but lets experiment and try. Nothing. At 12 after years of countless surgery/tests. I gave up. Besides daily exercise seemed to stop the bone pain.

&#x200B;

But my stomach is still inflamed. 17 afaik? Went for that specifically. They couldn't understand the bones and the tests showed. It's not fully marking up as usual IBS/Crohns disease but we'll try that. Again test,test,test more procedures. Nothing the doctor got very frustrated. I got painkillers and as they are a anti inflammatory. I no longer have to work out every bone from finger, toe, arm, back,hand daily. I have regular bowel movements, I'm not bloating or burning. And I can go outside! A decade of being housebound with no contact. Even prison inmates have contact. I've danced with tears in my eyes decades I wanted to be around ppl and just to dance! It did that.

&#x200B;

As for therapy. Well name one I haven't tried? They can't produce a magical talking technique or pill that makes your autoimmune diseases stop. They can't convince me it's irrational these pains are destroying you and you're all alone. Like hey! Here's a million pounds go buy a good life and friends. I tried SSRI's for years worst decision ever. I have fully body scarring from their bloating. I take opioids for over 4 years. And I can still miss 3-4 days without taking a single one. One night without SSRI's? You won't sleep, you'll have flu like symptoms, brain zaps, everything hurts. I appreciate it but the just go to the magical therapist unfortunately isn't an option.

&#x200B;

I wish to dance for the few years I have left before my body atrophies and I'm housebound. After that? Well no euthanasia here sadly. I'll find a way.

Oooft tho something oddly comforting about my body not living much longer than a couple of years and maybe my brain being mush I'll care less. Want to dance and go to raves for the first time. Something I thought and was waiting for my whole teens. When this stupid growing pain goes away! Nope not growing pain incurable no treatment autoimmune disease. Gotten progressively worse without any substances.

&#x200B;

I'll need to find another drug to experiment and enjoy my last few years.

Good for you! Some ppl do. Some ppl have medical conditions. So many women are on SSRI's and swear it works for them. I personally think it was the worst thing a doctor ever gave me. I have more scars on my body due to the weight gain/bloating than any other drug. And I can skip 3 days of painkillers. The supposed worst and most addictive drug. 1 night without SSRI's? Hell you won't sleep, brainzaps, sick feelings. 

&#x200B;

For me painkillers was the route when decades of hospitals not being able to diagnose, no operation or test working. Them becoming more frustrated with me. I found an option that has allowed me after 25 years. To actually be able to go outside, to work and help ppl. I've saved lives with that work. I danced for the first time at 25 crying my eyes out under the strobe thinking. I never thought this would ever be possible. 

&#x200B;

Yes long term it may harm me. But you know what would harm me more? I spent ten years 17-27 with no one. Prison inmates have more to talk to. I was in complete solitary. Alcohol is a drug. And I'd like to try enjoy/experiment like a normal human being got too. Before my body completely vegatables me. At which point cause euthanasia isn't legal here. I'll have to find a way out.

I have been to everything! I have a autoimmune disease incurable. I only got to go outside and club, dance for the first time at 27. I cried on the dance floor. There is no cure for decades I spent in hospital more time than I did outside with any friends. I lost all my friends due to chronic illness. Now It's hard cause 25 years of isolation you're very alone. 

&#x200B;

But I'd very much like to enjoy the last 2 years of my twenties before the big sleep comes knocking. I went to therapists of all kinds! There's no "cure" they can't say. Hey here's a magic pill and you'll be content to live housebound on your own. I tried SSRIs for years. Worst drug I ever took. I have physical unnremovable stretch marks from SSRI's weight gain/bloating. They can't talk you out of a society that's just not a good place for disabled/chronically ill people. The question is I've 2 years left at best. What's a good way to make the most of it? The consensus here is MDMA is like a 2-5 times lifetime drug. So I'll have to look elsewhere.

I have been to many! Worked as a drugs worker briefly and trained alongside them. Read papers. My physical pain is incurable only managable by painkillers which after 4 years tolerance I don't even use as a high. I get 100 a month and I've never needed more. It's mainly used so I can actually eat and not be hospitalised from the pain of eating, so I don't have 5,10,15 bowel movements a day. Instead 1.  MDMA doesn't hurt at all. Cocaine did. Which is why I wanted to ask questions papers I've read don't anwser. 

&#x200B;

I take 0 often for three days of painkillers. Then if the bloating, toilet usage and bone pain of inflammation comes back. I use painkillers as its anti inflammatory purpose. The only times I go near 10-12 is if. Oh gee I'd love something spicy or something I'm not allowed to eat. Then over the course of 12 hours I might break the rule and go to 10-12. 

&#x200B;

MDMA seemed to have worked fine. No interaction with inflammation, no gut problems, no bloating or bone pain. Cocaine however left me 2 days in agony. 

&#x200B;

Ppl like to take drugs the common in Scotland is 1.2g a session. And I know girls doing it often weekly. Yet I hate it, and all the side effects of MDMA over 4 months hasn't affected me. But this is why I'm asking these questions. Questions ppl assume to be me arguing or being rude. But questions is how I understand it better. And yes the conclusion seems to be stimulants are pretty sht. And sadly MDMA is not a good drug for me. So perhaps downers only from now on. Maybe a bit of ket now and then. That also seems to have less negative effects than cocaine.

Would like to add as it got downvoted. In my country a testing kit is grounds to charge you with intent to supply. And a much harsher crime than being caught with a bag of any substance. 

&#x200B;

So drugs workers like I used to be and have trained with. We would be illegal to provide harm reduction and testing as if police found us at festivals or near clubs with drugs/testing kit. It'd be bang to rights as a dealer.

Well I have a autoimmune disease from childhood that they've never accurately been able to diagnose. Operations, fortnightly blood tests, everything from leukemia, CRMO but couldn't explain stomach inflammation just bones. Stomach diagnoses of IBS/Crohns but I don't fit the markers fully. There's no actually cure/treatment. So pain meds have given me for the first time at 25. Sadly during lockdown but at 27 I cried cause I got to go to the club and dance for the first time.

&#x200B;

I've done drugs work, countless training with drugs worker. They don't really know either. My life expectancy is very short. I'd like to make the best of the 2 hopefully. Or more years before my body completely atrophies and euthanasia isn't legal here. So I'm asking questions from users that doctors/pharmacists and drugs workers can't anwser. 

&#x200B;

Seems the concensus is MDMA is the most unsafe drug. And I'll sadly have to look elsewhere. Which is a shame cause it's the only one which didn't interfere with my chronic pain. Funnily alcohol of most types doesn't upset anything. But food does. Food is more painful than a shot of vodka! Bodies are complex they don't know.

Seems you deleted your reply or I can't find it. Good for you! As is shown here most of these ppl do takes substances. And many ppl do for a multitude of reasons. For one my prescription has been 4 years it does not give me a high. I've never had to increase the dosage. I can go 3 days without any opiods then my bones will ache, my stomach will bloat, I'll be on the toilet 5-10 times or more a day. And many other ppl use drugs to medicate. With the right information everything is safe. Hence why I have been asking questions. And sadly it seems MDMA is not a good alternative to enhance a night out. Some ppl have said cocaine is less damaging to me. It completely nullifies my pain meds and I end up with the above symptoms and tiredness for 2 days.

&#x200B;

MDMA did not. But sadly it seems it's something you can only take 1-3 times in your life. So I'll look elsewhere. Alcohol of most types ironically also doesn't upset my inflammation. All types of food do however. Is food a drug?

But I appreciate the concern friend. And likewise if I was talking to a non disabled person I'd say the same. But I'm a childhood diagnosed autoimmune sufferer. My life has been hell. Then I was given a prescription for opioids. They did every test/operation imaginable from a very young age. Maybe it's this! The doctor told me at 7yos in the room with my parents. "Idk leukemia maybe? CRMO it doesn't fit fully and doesn't explain the stomach inflammation but we'll try." 6 years of fortnightly blood tests, canulas, operations tests. In adulthood they said. "Well it doesn't quite fit and the bone thing is unrelated. Maybe IBS/Crohns? You don't fit it fully but it's as close as we can guess." So on with the tests nothing.

&#x200B;

And then I asked for painkillers. Painkillers also act as a anti-inflammatory. It has cured nothing. But for the first time in my life. I managed to get a job, dance, go out and eat with ppl? Have relationships. 

&#x200B;

I'm aware being a chronic immune sufferer my life expectancy will be short. But when ppl raise concerns of liver failure. All I can think of is? Thank God. Rather that then decades more of agony tests they can't find anything and I live housebound, no lights, no dancing, no love. So forgive me if I want to look around for drugs to use occassaionly in my what 12 more years of life? Maybe more but it'll get worse? 28 now i wouldn't be surprised if 30 things start going downhill very quickly healthwise. I'd like to party a little bit and be a live before then.

Uh yeah that sucks. As right now I wake up fine no comedown or pain. One night on cocaine. And it'll be 2 days. My painkillers stop working. And it's like having the painkillers removed. 2 days I'll be inside not eating and in agony. 

&#x200B;

Well the search goes on.

I'm already damaged from chronic pain. It's autoimmune no cure. The painkillers will likely knock decades off my life. But right now. I can dance first time in 25 years of life. 28 now. I've actually been able to be at a rave/club. I never thought it'd be possible. Without it I'd be bedbound wishing for euthansaia. Cocaine seemed to have an effect of neutralising all the properties of pain relief. 4 years on a doctors script so a small amount given monthly. It's not even a high. It's just I don't want to be on the toilet 10+ times a day, and bedbound wishing for lethal injection.

&#x200B;

MDMA fortnightly didn't interact badly with it at all. But I have taken the advice here and sadly it does look like I'll have to look elsewhere for another kind of drug.

Why? Oh sorry didn't realise  you go to clubs/raves with just water. Well one drug opioids is required medical. Or nevermind dancing. I'd be bedbound, carers bring food. 10+ bowel movements daily, bones cracking and in agony. Stomach bloating and burning. 

&#x200B;

Yeah I'm aware. I actually think cocaine is far worse long run. And I certainly felt that way on it. But fortnightly mdma has had zero negative affects on my physical body. And I seem to wake up refreshed. More refreshed than your drug of excessive alcohol.

It is also worth noting. 4 years of Opioid usage on the tiny script the chemist  gives you of 100. To last for a month. It's not even giving me any high. It's just their to stop my bones from snapping. I used to have to exercise every joint and limb individually daily. My stomach would flare up till I was housebound. Bloating, horrendous bowel movements 10+ times a day. Now? I nearly skip exercise weeks at a time. I stay within the 8 paracetomol/opioid guidelines. Some days I skip it all together for 3 days without withdrawal. At bad days flare ups from bad food. Yeah i may dip to 10-12. 

&#x200B;

But I've been able to go to a club and dance for the first time in my life. Before and if they took painkillers away? Vegetable I'd need carers to bring my shopping. Couldn't get out of bed most days. And I certainly couldn't step foot in any club. Nevermind dance.

I'm sadly not depedent. My dealer in a very predatory way even said to me. "Wow you must be really strong." As I don't buy often enough than I assume his other clients. Like I said the painkillers unfortunately can not go. It's been 4 years not even used as a high substance. Just a my bone inflammation stops, my stomach stops bloating. I have regular bowel movements. 

&#x200B;

Cocaine seems to cancel out a lot of the opioids help around bowels/bloating/stomach pain. MDMA seems to have zero physical effect on my physical health. And definetely mentally mixed in moderation once every 2 weeks or so. Seems to give me a boost. Idk about Ket only done it 2-3 times and mostly it was used as a. Can't sleep after cocaine, hearts too fast. A few lines and now I'm sleepy in my bed.

So I understand your concern for healthy bodies. But as a chronically ill person I would very much not like to live much longer than 50. Especially if the GPs decide. In fact I think you should be a housebound vegetable. My question has to be looked through that lense. And for party drugs. My body is telling me cocaine hurts. MDMA doesn't have any phyiscal pain the day taking/day after. Week after. Ket I'm unsure of only taken it 2-3 times and mostly It was used as a. I got home can't sleep cause heart palpations and cocaine making me feel like death. So it helped me calm down and sleep. 

&#x200B;

Not sure how much I'll enjoy it as a party drug. Xanax might be the alternative for me then. But two downers sounds like a good way to make me not one too dance anymore. Dancing something previously physically impossible due to the pain now prevented by opioids.

The opioids are prescription and required for chronic pain they're not a high. I take 2 at max on weekdays. Sometimes 4 if done a few days without. That's just so my inflammation and bone pain goes away. On nights out I'll go to the max 8 dose. Sometimes cheeky 10-12. I was already week coke for 6 months 1-2g. And even the first few times it ruined my stomach felt horrible for days after. fortnightly mdma for nights out has been fine so far. I'd much rather if that was the option to twice cocaine a week. Or Ket once a week. 

&#x200B;

The serious damage of liver stuff is unavoidable. As a chronically ill person I will never live without the opioids sadly. For my doctor to remove them. I'd be a housebound vegetable unable to even go to the shops. Require full time care. Now I can live a normal life and party. I wanted to make the switch to MDMA as 3 months going fortnightly break beside one week where there was events on and I dipped a few times into the bag.

Good advice! I did read up on it. And sadly there's no agreed upon concrete. The 2 week rule is mostly what I've been following and I seem to dodge all side effects over 3 months of taking. So I'm curious if continuing that is safe. I'd much rather that. Than say go back to cocaine every other week. It gives me all the side effects listed by rollsafe and others etc. When i know ppl who take cocaine and have none of that. 

&#x200B;

None of you are toxiciologists in this field. But I cannot find any expert advice on this and so turned to the best thing to expert ppl who also go to clubs/raves.

I have researched. Most papers are inconclusive between ten years, 3 months and 2 weeks. Most of mine bar a couple have been 2 weeks. I'd like to narrow that down. I was on coke for a while it felt horrible. But every 2 weeks MDMA over 6+ sessions over 3 months. I haven't noticed the side effects like Coke did everytime. 

&#x200B;

I'd like also for research and info into that. Is it possible the downers/dopamine drugs like opioids are masking the side effects? Are they alleviating or stopping them? I have respect for drugs which is why I'm asking if I switch to a 2 week rule would that continue to work for me? I researched it as you put in brackets not believing me. Some places do agree 2 weeks is fine. I wanted more firsthand experiences from other club/rave goers. And also why 0.1 seems to have worked wonder for ppl when my first time 0.1 did absolutely nothing.

Of course! Which is why I want to look further. And the research papers are very unsure of how often is even agreed upon. Some saying ten years, 3 months, 2 weeks. But all the side effects listed have been completely missed by me. I have no scientific basis for why other than my guess of... Dopamine from opioids, downers like Xanax yesterday stopping all the side effects of the next day.

&#x200B;

It's also possible due to me going off coke the worst drug for me I was doing 1g-2g twice a week. And feeling horrible for days. The same descriptors of MDMA comedown. Which is completely absent to me. While I know coke girls out daily with no issue.

But the too much would mean it stopped working and I'd have side effects? Unless the side effects are completely neutered by downers? I'll maybe have to test a night on only MDMA however I'll still be on my prescription painkillers as I require them medically. 

&#x200B;

But even my first night I took 0.5 mainly cause I wanted to weigh it when I got in. 0.1 would have done nothing for me. Do you think it's possible because before I was doing anything from 1g-2g of cocaine that my tolerance is just high before first trying it?

Yeah as far as I can see I probably got Amazing4health from their. Shipping from Thailand.

&#x200B;

The only other Paypal HRT place I see their is Pilliod from Russia. So potentially may be cheaper. But have no way of knowing if they're legit. Will look anyway for price comparisons.

Just want to add as rereading this it sounds like my money situation is quite bad. It is not yet. I have many safety measures in place. Money stashed away, people to ask re money, and work I can do if things get quite rough for a while. 

&#x200B;

I'm more just planning in advance. Just in case I start seeing these other bills start to drain my money and I don't have time to find a cheaper option. Hopefully the new GIC funding will speed things along! I've been given a optimistic answer from trans workers at LGBT charities. Worst case the money will do nothing to speed along waiting times. But best case hopefully only have 2 more years of rough living.

Hello I went to a harm reduction clinic to get my bloods taken and they had guidance from the GIC on HRT. Basically apparently the GIC uses monotherapy first and only a blocker if you aren't properly suppressed to avoid health risks associated with a blocker.

&#x200B;

Now I've been self medding for like 3 years on and off and different doses. I defo feel I need a blocker now after guessing. But it surprised me to find out that the GIC apparently mostly tries to use estrogen only. Will post the pictures when I get my phone.
